  "query_preview": "..\ncurrently there are areas of low clouds and what appears to be\npatchy fog. We will continue to monitor overnight if fog \ncoverage increases, especially along the travel corridors. Best \nchance for fog development will be in the higher valleys south \nand east of Tucson, especially along the I-10 Corridor. Any fog \nwill quickly diminish shortly after sunrise. \n\nFriday into Saturday it will be an open wave and move through \nnorthern Arizona or southern Utah, still uncertainty on how far \nsouth it will travel. Right now southeast Arizona is expected to\nbe dry when this system moves through with rain chances staying\nfurther north. Winds may also be a little breezy Friday \nafternoon. However the upper air pattern stays progressive with \nensembles bringing another trough through the region early next \nweek. This trough looks to have a more southerly trajectory and \ncould bring rain chances Monday. NBM PoPs are currently 10-25 \npercent.\n\nTemperatures will follow the roller coaster of below normal to \nslight above normal for the week due to the passing weather \nsystems.",
